{"availability":"available","full":"Aryabhatta-0/Wynk","name":"Wynk","description":"An efficient search system for agentic workflows","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":6,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T06:23:19Z","updated":"2026-10-07T12:21:57Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ui-ten-virid.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://ui-ten-virid.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T10:25:01.002Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T10:25:01.002Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T10:25:01.002Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T10:25:01.002Z","discoveredVia":[{"kind":"x","name":"As Seen On X.com","url":"https://x.com/i/web/status/2108255200779874616","postId":"2108255200779874616","postedAt":"2026-10-08T17:56:24.000Z"}],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T10:25:01.002Z","stars":6,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Wynk is a search system for agentic workflows. Instead of a human hand-writing the pipeline for an agent task, Wynk represents a workflow as a genome — an ordered tuple of typed stages — and searches the space of genomes with ant-colony optimisation, scored by a deterministic evaluator.","The bet: the win is not only which steps you run, but which steps you leave out. Turning every stage on makes a pipeline heavier, slower, and easier to fail (see the full-pipeline ablation). Wynk's advantage comes from choosing a per-task-class structure.","The project is research-grade: it runs end-to-end against a real hosted Gemma model, and every result below is reproducible from frozen artifacts."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Aryabhatta-0/Wynk/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ff24ac80a008891286cc436e00390dd7085c2f04e2f0b96b36088919bc2f6863","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T07:21:59.039Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T10:25:01.002Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Wynk is a search system for agentic workflows. Instead of a human hand-writing th